  "title": "GLM-5.3 crossed a new cyber capability threshold",
  "narration": "Anthropic says GLM-5.3 crossed a serious cyber capability threshold. In its tests, the model built end-to-end exploits autonomously. Useful for defenders, and obviously awkward for everyone else. On ExploitBench, it succeeded in 50 of 410 attempts. Anthropic also tested how easily safeguards could be bypassed. Simple techniques worked between 64 and 100 percent of the time. That combination is the uncomfortable part. Strong exploit development is reaching downloadable models. NIST separately called GLM-5.3 the most cyber-capable open-weight model yet. This is not proof of automatic real-world attacks. But security teams have less time before advanced techniques spread. Open weights just made the clock much louder.",
